    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but thats what i dont get. why does it have to be a \"journey\" if the destination is always just more pain? like i've done the therapy, i've tried the meds, i've tried all the \"coping skills\"... and i still feel like a shattered glass. it's not like i can just glue myself back together. some things just can't be fixed.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely valid to feel that the path is a dead end when the pain never ends, and no amount of \"fixing\" seems to work. You are right to feel frustrated that the destination isn't relief, and it is unfair that you have to carry such a heavy burden alone. But please remember that healing with \"shattered glass\" rarely fits a traditional roadmap or a time frame we have been given.",
      "source": "target",
